WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.202
Okay, we're here on CNN
with the co-author of the book,

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.004
 The Canceling
 of the American Mind,

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.172
-Greg Lukianoff.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:09.508
CNN senior political analyst
and anchor, John Avlon,

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:12.178
and special correspondent
for PBS NewsHour,

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.446
Jane Ferguson.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.381
Okay, here are the questions.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:19.285
That the people of America
want to know of our CNN panel.

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:20.753
You're often
on a CNN panel, right?

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.821
Yes, I am.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.590
Okay, so this
is just new to you,
not new to you.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.860
What does the panel think
of choosing Taylor Swift

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.995
as Time Magazine Person
of the Year?

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:31.831
One hundred percent for it.
She totally deserves it.

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:35.668
-I'm not kidding. (CHUCKLES)
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:41.941
No, I mean, yeah, who can argue?

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.276
It was her and the cat, though.
The cat should get credit.

00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:46.045
-BILL MAHER: Well, she's--
I mean--
-(ALL CHUCKLING)

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:47.813
It's a phenomenal year.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.083
I mean, we have not seen a year
like that in show business,

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:51.684
maybe ever.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:55.388
What are the panel's thoughts
on Hunter Biden being indicted?

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.959
-Hey, look...
-(ALL LAUGH)

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:01.961
BILL: Why ask? (LAUGHS)

00:01:03.662 --> 00:01:05.531
It just shows
that the equal justice

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:06.599
under law exists.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.035
The president's son, you know,
is gonna get busted

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:12.171
for evading taxes and you know,
he did it in a lot of...

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.440
A moment of grief
and that doesn't really matter

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.943
because you gotta obey the law
no matter whose son you are.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.377
-No matter who...
-BILL: It does really...

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:19.745
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.281
JOHN AVLON: We've got
a two-tier justice system.

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:26.619
It does really point out
that one side does consider

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.821
the law a little more
seriously than the other.

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:31.657
And the fact that they kind of
compare it to Trump,

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.793
like Hunter Biden
is not our hero.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:34.927
(GREG LUKIANOFF LAUGHS)

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.830
-Okay?
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:42.968
Okay, what kind of interference
can we expect from Russia

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:46.139
-as the 2024 election heats up?
-JANE FERGUSON: None needed.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:49.542
-Well, but...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.143
JOHN: No, but...

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:52.912
-Unfortunately.
-Sadly, it's true.

00:01:53.078 --> 00:01:55.381
But actually there's a story
that just came out yesterday

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.617
in the UK but the US
was involved as well,

00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:58.818
that Russia
is doing cyber hacking

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.519
specifically with the goal

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.922
of not only disrupting
their election,

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:06.492
but eroding faith
in democracy itself.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.294
And I think
that's the larger stakes.

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:09.862
And we've seen this on TikTok,

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.030
a lot of these things
that go viral.

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:12.131
You've discussed that.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.734
You know, and now,
you see, Xi--

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.269
You know, Trump losing
no opportunity to praise Xi

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:18.805
in every campaign speech.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:21.106
You know, the guy,
Donald Trump loves dictators,

00:02:21.206 --> 00:02:22.574
but I think
that dramatically increases

00:02:22.641 --> 00:02:24.176
the chance of interference

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:25.811
only because people
are gonna want...

00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:28.414
Those autocratic alternatives
are gonna want to degrade

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.749
democracy and put us
on a path towards decline.

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:33.019
But are we flattering ourselves
in thinking that

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:35.354
that's what they need to do
as opposed to sit back

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.223
-and watch? I mean, like...
-No.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.059
There was, of course,
the misinformation campaign

00:02:40.125 --> 00:02:41.427
-and bots on Twitter.
-JOHN: Yeah.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.296
Making us all get outraged
and row and fight.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:47.199
But it feels like
that's taken on an organic life
of its own now.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.168
And perhaps we're flattering
ourselves by saying,

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.703
"It must be an interference."

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.872
We see this in other parts
of the world

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:56.341
you know, whenever people
rise up against, you know,

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:58.845
their leaders and everyone says
it's a conspiracy.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:02.114
By all means, Russia will
and would love to interfere.

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:03.849
-They are.
-I kind of wonder if,
like, these days,

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:04.984
they really need to.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.420
I mean, this election
is not looking too tight.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.822
-Yeah.
-Yeah. In canceling,
we talk a lot

00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:11.457
about what experts have done
to undermine

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.360
their own credibility,
unfortunately, in recent years.

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.061
And that's also a big thing
that Russia's trying

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.563
to do as well.
And unfortunately,

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.032
they're like, you know,
they're complimenting each other

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.333
in the worst possible way.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.905
Okay, what did the panel think
of Vivek Ramaswamy's

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.440
performance at the debate
this week?

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:30.476
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.644
I had to watch that?

00:03:32.911 --> 00:03:35.114
-Yeah. I did.
-BILL: Did you watch? Oh.

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:36.416
(LAUGHS)

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:39.318
-It's not on the test, Greg.
-(ALL LAUGH)

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.586
If you didn't see it, it was--

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.888
In one answer,
he managed to connect

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:45.424
every conspiracy theory
from the 21st century.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.526
-GREG: Well, that's cool.
-From 9/11.

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:49.328
Well, except,
it was clearly a dog whistle

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.997
to folks on the far right
to sort of connect 9/11,

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:54.801
say January 6th
was an inside job,

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.969
to talk about
the great replacement theory

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.906
and saying there was
a Democratic Party platform.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.575
And to say-- and to repeat
2020 election lies,

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.076
which are now a litmus test
within the party.

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:06.745
That symbolizes everything wrong
in our politics.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:08.780
It's totally disgusting.
It's disqualifying.

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:10.883
It's pathetic
and it's pandering. He's done.

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.652
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:16.622
-I should've gone with him.
-It pisses me off.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:20.626
I think it also, though,
really speaks
to a level of desperation.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:23.162
I mean, you have to be
pretty scared

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:24.997
to start connecting
more and more,

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.965
and more
conspiracy theories together.

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:29.702
I mean, there's got to be like
a limit to where, you know,

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.638
once you've had too many
then you really look

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:33.806
like you're losing.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.107
GREG: Gotta work in pizzagate.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:38.344
-Right.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.413
Well, he did
with the Chris Christie joke.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.482
-Oh, did he really?
-Well, he worked in pizza.

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:45.718
-(ALL LAUGH)
-There's something.
Didn't he say something?

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:49.956
I mean, he made,
he made a fat joke

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.124
at Chris Christie.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.526
I just want to--
I tried to like this guy.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.895
I had him on my podcast.
Had him on the show.

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.397
-He's a personable guy.
-GREG: Mm-hmm.

00:04:57.597 --> 00:05:01.000
But I just got to say,
youth shows itself.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.268
I mean, he kept saying--
The debates I watched,

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:05.271
he kept saying,
it's time for a new generation,

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:07.440
which they all say
when the young guy comes along.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.308
And this just showed, it's not.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:11.977
-Because this generation...
-Not that guy.

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.914
What? Well, not that guy.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:18.317
Because it just showed,
you know, come back--

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:23.188
My advice to them, stop.
Just stop it. Go away.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:26.259
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-Come back. He's 38 years old.

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.628
Come back in ten
or 20 years and say,

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:29.728
"Oh yeah, you know what?

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:31.730
I can't believe I did
what I did when I was 38."

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:34.433
-'Cause we can all relate
to that.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.202
And like, I just--
Run for office,

00:05:37.269 --> 00:05:39.872
not just straight for president
'cause you want to get famous.

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:41.474
'Cause, you know,
your idiocy is showing.

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:44.777
I mean, it also just seems
so performative. I get it.

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:47.079
What he's thinking is,
the Republican party

00:05:47.145 --> 00:05:49.181
likes dicks. It does.

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:50.716
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:05:50.882 --> 00:05:52.785
But you know,
with Trump it's authentic.

00:05:53.385 --> 00:05:55.154
-(JOHN LAUGHING)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:57.322
Now, you're kind of
complimenting him.

00:05:57.389 --> 00:05:59.558
-He's not really a dick, but...
-BILL: He's not.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.393
-...he's trying to be one.
-I think he's playing one.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.363
-JOHN: That's almost worse.
-That's al-- Exactly.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:08.334
It is worse. It's almost worse.
Trump can't help being a dick.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:09.635
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:14.707
This guy is playing one.
Also, I must tell you.

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:19.144
A number of Indian-Americans
I know who are friends of mine

00:06:19.211 --> 00:06:20.812
have said, "Bill,
please tell America,

00:06:20.879 --> 00:06:22.115
he does not represent us."

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.649
You know, that's like,
that's a bad guy

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:24.817
to go out first.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:26.285
-But there's Nikki Haley.
-JOHN: You got Nikki Haley.

00:06:26.351 --> 00:06:29.522
Who, you know, like,
do I agree with everything? No.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:32.959
But could I easily live under
Nikki Haley's America? Yes.

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:35.027
And I might even enjoy it.
I don't know.

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:36.895
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:06:37.195 --> 00:06:40.533
This is all--
What's going to happen
in the next two months

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.569
between Iowa and New Hampshire
is going to be enormously--

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:44.937
I mean, this is a time
for choosing.

00:06:45.003 --> 00:06:48.007
Republicans have one last chance
to not renominate someone

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:49.809
who tried to overturn
our democracy.

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:52.444
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING, CHEERING)

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:55.314
Okay, Jane...

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:58.351
Are there--
Dublin is your hometown?

00:06:58.618 --> 00:07:01.087
-Well, New York City.
-(JOHN LAUGHS)

00:07:01.253 --> 00:07:03.489
I come from Northern Ireland,
just north of the border.

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:05.891
-BILL: Oh, Northern Ireland.
-JANE: It's complex.

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:08.594
Yes. Oh, I know.

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.996
Are the riots in Dublin a sign

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:14.132
that extremist politics
are gaining a foothold

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:15.234
in Ireland?

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.236
Okay, so explain what--
I read it,

00:07:17.302 --> 00:07:18.971
-but you have to explain it.
-JANE: It's pretty wild.

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:20.773
So, Ireland, I mean,

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:23.075
I had to reread
the story several times.

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:24.576
BILL: It was about Musk,
wasn't it?

00:07:24.776 --> 00:07:28.948
No, It was really kind of,
it's a fomenting of a sort of

00:07:29.781 --> 00:07:31.884
very, very tiny minority
that's very loud

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.251
and very violent.

00:07:33.652 --> 00:07:36.889
That it basically, it's,
you know, anti-immigration

00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:40.392
and it's all the usual populist
kind of conversation.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.127
-I think the fact--
-But what stirred them up?

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:44.963
Wasn't it something on Twitter?
I refuse to call it X.

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:48.200
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:53.506
A lot of it comes down
to like rumors

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:56.542
and misinformation and it--
but it's grounded.

00:07:56.675 --> 00:07:59.145
And so, Twitter's a big,
big part of that there

00:07:59.345 --> 00:08:00.346
in this case. But--

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:02.047
BILL: But Twitter's better,
isn't it?

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:04.883
I feel like it's so much easier
to go, "Twitter."

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:07.220
I refuse to call it X.
Than go, "X formally Twitter."

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:08.553
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:08:08.787 --> 00:08:10.289
X used to be a drug. You know?

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:12.158
That's what people used to,
you know--

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:14.260
I'm also going
to call Kanye, Kanye.

00:08:14.426 --> 00:08:15.894
I'm not going to go with Ye.

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:19.131
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-The people....

00:08:19.364 --> 00:08:20.633
The Irish thing though.

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:23.402
I mean, honestly,
like, the thing that concerns me

00:08:23.468 --> 00:08:26.172
is that whenever you start
having a pretty sort of violent,

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:29.575
extremely right wing
riot in Ireland,

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:32.177
I mean, this is just,
this is unprecedented.

00:08:32.244 --> 00:08:33.312
BILL: We've had them here.

00:08:33.445 --> 00:08:35.514
JANE: But yeah,
I mean, never in Ireland.

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:38.617
Like, I mean Ireland is,
so antithetical to everything.

00:08:38.717 --> 00:08:39.952
You know, we know about--

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:42.855
Ireland was the first country
to-- by popular vote,

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:44.724
legalize gay marriage, you know.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.825
I mean, Ireland is one
of the most liberal places.

00:08:46.892 --> 00:08:48.661
Well, kind of late
in the game though.

00:08:48.727 --> 00:08:52.264
-A lot has changed.
A lot has changed.
-What year was that?

00:08:52.898 --> 00:08:55.501
That was fifteen years ago,
ten years ago.

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:57.036
That's kind of late in the game.

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:58.937
All right, raise a glass
to Shane MacGowan, by the way,

00:08:59.004 --> 00:09:01.340
-speaking of Ireland.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:09:01.406 --> 00:09:02.708
-BILL: Wait, what?
-GREG: But I will say...

00:09:02.775 --> 00:09:04.042
Lead singer of the Pogues died.

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:07.413
The attempt to ban hate speech
in Ireland,

00:09:07.546 --> 00:09:08.814
that got passed recently.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.851
I see the same thing
going on in France.

00:09:11.917 --> 00:09:13.351
And they can't seem
to understand that they passed

00:09:13.418 --> 00:09:16.155
these anti-Semitism laws
in the '90s and somehow

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:17.590
anti-Semitism got worse.

00:09:17.657 --> 00:09:19.925
And it's because you told
all the anti-Semites

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:22.260
that they can only talk
to other anti-Semites.

00:09:22.494 --> 00:09:23.996
What did you expect to happen?

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:26.465
And this is actually
the same thing
on college campuses.

00:09:26.665 --> 00:09:28.600
When students are not talking
to one another.

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:30.636
They're not like having
civil discourse.

00:09:30.802 --> 00:09:31.803
Opinions don't go away

00:09:31.937 --> 00:09:33.706
-'cause you ban someone
saying them.
-GREG: Exactly.

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:36.741
We need to get, like,
especially students on campus,

00:09:36.842 --> 00:09:39.277
make them sit down and talk.
Make them debate.

00:09:39.344 --> 00:09:41.513
And make them say this
to each other's faces.

00:09:41.646 --> 00:09:43.181
This is one
of the most important things

00:09:43.248 --> 00:09:44.583
that your show's
doing right now.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.351
Which is defining
liberal values.

00:09:46.418 --> 00:09:48.954
And saying, "We need to stand up
against liberalism on the left

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.022
as well as the right."

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:51.456
And there's a group
of common sense Democrats,

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:53.759
liberal patriots,
radical centrists,

00:09:53.826 --> 00:09:56.028
that need to start taking
the conversation back.

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:58.297
Well said. Thank you, everybody.

00:09:58.364 --> 00:10:00.733
-We'll see you next week
for our season finale.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

